<title>USA: Freddie Mac to pay interest on debentures.</title>
<headline>Freddie Mac to pay interest on debentures.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Home Loan Mortgage Corp on Tuesday said it set an interest payment schedule for debentures as follows.</p>
<p>								     Interest</p>
<p>								     Payment</p>
<p>   Principal  Rate  Maturity    Cusip    Interest    Date</p>
<p>$ 50 million  5.72  04/22/03  3134A0E40 $286,458.33  09/23/96*</p>
<p>$ 50 million  6.47  04/26/01  3134A0E73 $269,583.33  09/26/96*</p>
<p>$ 50 million  5.72  02/26/03  3134A0VX7 $206,802.54  09/26/96#</p>
<p>$100 million  6.65  03/28/03  3134A0ZM7 $477,179.94  09/30/96##</p>
<p>*Current factor 1.00000000. No principal redeemed with interest. Outstanding principal balance $50 million.</p>
<p>#Partial principal redemption of $831,259.45 redeemed with interest payment. Current factor is 0.851077791. Factor applicable to principal redemption 0.016625189. Outstanding principal balance $42,553,889.56.</p>
<p>##Principal payment of $1,651,200.47 redeemed with interest payment. Current factor 0.844564586. Outstanding principal balance $84,456,458.58.</p>
